# Converted from tests/test_dfc_ev1_conformance.c test /file-number-out-of-range (now removed): the literal
# APDUs and statuses the unit test asserted are replayed here byte for byte,
# and the engine's answers are the ones the test required. File number 0x20 is a parameter error for record, value and transaction MAC files too (the standard data file case is ev1_file-number-out-of-range.vec); once file 1 exists, creating it again as another family is a duplicate, except a transaction MAC file whose creation is a parameter error.

name: vecB ev1: file number 0x20 across file families
case-id: vecb-ev1-file-number-out-of-range-families
origin: synthetic
requires: transaction-mac
source: tests/test_dfc_ev1_conformance.c /file-number-out-of-range
uid: 04A1B2C3D4E5F6
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-key-len: 16

scan
status   90CA0000050102030F0100 => 00
status   905A00000301020300 => 00
status   90C100000A2000EEEE01000002000000 => 9E
status   90CC0000112000EEEE0000000000000000000000000000 => 9E
status   90CE0000162000EEEF02000000000000000000000000000000000000 => 9E
status   90CD0000070100EEEE01000000 => 00
status   90C100000A0100EEEE01000002000000 => DE
status   90CC0000110100EEEE0000000000000000000000000000 => DE
status   90CE0000160100EEEF02000000000000000000000000000000000000 => 9E
assert   credential.num_files = 1
